.TH SDL_Folder 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_Folder \- The type of the OS-provided default folder for a specific purpose.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_filesystem.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef enum SDL_Folder
.BI "{
.BI "    SDL_FOLDER_HOME,        /**< The folder which contains all of the current user's data, preferences, and documents. It usually contains most of the other folders. If a requested folder does not exist, the home folder can be considered a safe fallback to store a user's documents. */
.BI "    SDL_FOLDER_DESKTOP,     /**< The folder of files that are displayed on the desktop. Note that the existence of a desktop folder does not guarantee that the system does show icons on its desktop; certain GNU/Linux distros with a graphical environment may not have desktop icons. */
.BI "    SDL_FOLDER_DOCUMENTS,   /**< User document files, possibly application-specific. This is a good place to save a user's projects. */
.BI "    SDL_FOLDER_DOWNLOADS,   /**< Standard folder for user files downloaded from the internet. */
.BI "    SDL_FOLDER_MUSIC,       /**< Music files that can be played using a standard music player (mp3, ogg...). */
.BI "    SDL_FOLDER_PICTURES,    /**< Image files that can be displayed using a standard viewer (png, jpg...). */
.BI "    SDL_FOLDER_PUBLICSHARE, /**< Files that are meant to be shared with other users on the same computer. */
.BI "    SDL_FOLDER_SAVEDGAMES,  /**< Save files for games. */
.BI "    SDL_FOLDER_SCREENSHOTS, /**< Application screenshots. */
.BI "    SDL_FOLDER_TEMPLATES,   /**< Template files to be used when the user requests the desktop environment to create a new file in a certain folder, such as \(dqNew Text File.txt\(dq.  Any file in the Templates folder can be used as a starting point for a new file. */
.BI "    SDL_FOLDER_VIDEOS,      /**< Video files that can be played using a standard video player (mp4, webm...). */
.BI "    SDL_FOLDER_COUNT        /**< Total number of types in this enum, not a folder type by itself. */
.BI "} SDL_Folder;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Note that the Trash folder isn\(aqt included here, because trashing files usually involves extra OS-specific functionality to remember the file\(aqs original location\[char46]
.PP
The folders supported per platform are:
.PP
|             | Windows | macOS/iOS | tvOS | Unix (XDG) | Haiku | Emscripten | | ----------- | ------- | --------- | ---- | ---------- | ----- | ---------- | | HOME        | X       | X         |      | X          | X     | X          | | DESKTOP     | X       | X         |      | X          | X     |            | | DOCUMENTS   | X       | X         |      | X          |       |            | | DOWNLOADS   | Vista+  | X         |      | X          |       |            | | MUSIC       | X       | X         |      | X          |       |            | | PICTURES    | X       | X         |      | X          |       |            | | PUBLICSHARE |         | X         |      | X          |       |            | | SAVEDGAMES  | Vista+  |           |      |            |       |            | | SCREENSHOTS | Vista+  |           |      |            |       |            | | TEMPLATES   | X       | X         |      | X          |       |            | | VIDEOS      | X       | X*        |      | X          |       |            |
.PP
Note that on macOS/iOS, the Videos folder is called \(dqMovies\(dq\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This enum is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_GetUserFolder (3)
